<description>&lt;p&gt;US authorities have taken a fugitive businessman into custody in Venezuela on bribery charges while Maduro and Cilia Flores face formal US accusations of ordering torture, prompting protests. An aid worker reports shocking earthquake damage in Venezuela and Rubio urges all opposition figures to join talks with the government. Starlink internet is now permitted to operate in Venezuela and Cuba’s grid collapse is worsening regional strain, while energy firms are recruiting former US officials to access Venezuelan oil and charges allege a PDVSA plane was used to transport goods. The UCDP recorded 2 battle-related deaths in 2007.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiwwFBVV95cUxOX0dPTzMxQmZlR2ROS0E2T3czWFg4ZVNHb1A3NG9fdmFsQzdhSG5YOTBMVHgxZzEyeTJpaWZYMHNuaW52WlZmNHItb1hmR2xha1ZtemVjSkw4U2psUzdNRVFGTmFUQXVJRmJudGVPMzFSRnFtSUhrQ1F3b3lvTERwVjI1VkkzUXZnaUo5U2Z3ZWRxNnl4S1ppRFJ6RlJ3WkZUNFpjZkM2OUw0NnV4MG5yUVQ1Zms0N25od1NySEZIUERMMjg?oc=5&quot;&gt;The New York Times&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiXkFVX3lxTE9LSF9RZW5GTEdOektnanhEMFJpbHFuRXJ1T0tGVUczVFBYNl9wMTRBZXF5SE90Z1BZdzJxc3FBMzRKaHVleWFydWhLVGVQTGdJVUd3aUpXUEFlcllnbmc?oc=5&quot;&gt;BBC&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Raw Story&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiyAFBVV95cUxPVFVLSUpkSmg4bVVpRXpuSkJ2SGl6eU9Xa2ZNZ09EaUVkZ1c5Q1NyR1ZHWkk1OFVyWHpCSlhYekVGb2RWdGdmc1I2WGk1T2dzZmlZMnNTX3dZV3ZYNVZNZ0JVMF90eDZya0tSTGpPLXdzTVNLS2E4NWVzMGs5SFJTM1A5WExzbmR4ZlY1ekJCRHgxbEhyZ0RsbC1EcjZRZ1JsYnNieE9lYzd2NWVFTXFJc00xUGFXTTVENmhLUjNmTFliYWlQejRBaA?oc=5&quot;&gt;Monthly Review&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMingFBVV95cUxOODd5cGlHZUM3UVJmeUVYdWRzRGRSeGs2UHdSTW1sMHhNSnZxMjZmTHlXSmVvNWxCZXRIeTBQUEt5RXBMUnEwUUVTYU5YTDlrZE95Zm16bU10cD